From: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: select the started netdev queue for monitor TX

Monitor open starts netdev queue zero. The ordinary selector has no monitor
case, marks the skb as having no station, and returns the BCMC netdev queue.
That queue remains stopped after the managed interface was closed. Diagnostic
packet sends fill the socket buffer (93 packets) and then return EAGAIN.

Select queue zero and retain the no-station priority for the monitor callback,
which uses the unknown-vif firmware TX queue. Limit the change to the compiled
experimental monitor TX path. Managed/AP queues keep their original selection.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
---
 USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/aic8800-usb-5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-7/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c b/usr/src/aic8800-usb-5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-7/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
--- a/usr/src/aic8800-usb-5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-7/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
+++ b/usr/src/aic8800-usb-5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-7/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
@@ -304,6 +304,12 @@ u16 rwnx_select_txq(struct rwnx_vif *rwnx_vif, struct sk_buff *skb)
     }
 
     switch (wdev->iftype) {
+#ifdef CONFIG_RWNX_MON_XMIT
+    case NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR:
+        /* Monitor open starts queue zero; do not use the stopped BCMC queue. */
+        skb->priority = PRIO_STA_NULL;
+        return 0;
+#endif
     case NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION:
     case NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_CLIENT:
     {
